FI - END ONE IF LEVEL

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
FI - END ONE IF LEVEL

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

Syntax:
    FI

Closes the current conditional level and returns to its parent. Each
nested IF needs its own FI.

Example: IF NULL;ECHO HELLO;FI

Use IFQ to inspect the conditional state if a command seems to be skipped.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
